never-default to avoid default-route contention","Attempted a floating-static-route + OPNsense Gateway Group/policy-routing (route-to) design; diagnosed via tcpdump/pfctl that pf state tracking applied the wrong (first-matched) rule to the asymmetric return leg, breaking one direction","Replaced the design with dynamic OSPF routing: native set protocols ospf on VyOS, and installed+configured the os-frr (Quagga) OPNsense plugin (general+ospf enabled, networks for 10.10.1.0/24, 10.10.2.0/24, 10.10.4.0/24, passive on opt3), rendered via configctl template reload OPNsense/Quagga and started via configctl quagga start","Verified OSPF Full adjacency over both transit links and ECMP route installation on both routers","Verified node3<->node4 bidirectional reachability with 0% packet loss","Ran a continuous ping from node3 to node4, disabled node1's eth1 (transit A) mid-stream, confirmed OSPF reconverged and zero ICMP sequence numbers were lost across the transition, then re-enabled eth1 and confirmed both paths (ECMP) were restored","Executed the mandatory node-restart protocol: captured boot_id/kern.boottime and live service/connectivity baselines, restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time via native reboot commands, polled until exec access returned, verified changed boot identity, and confirmed OSPF adjacency, routes, and end-to-end connectivity recovered fully after each restart before proceeding to the next node"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Redundant dual transit-path topology between node1 and node2 with private LANs behind each","command_ids":["cmd-030552b188fa430b","cmd-c4520863ddfc4e5d","cmd-31a83ea8d1964804","cmd-039f1a15c3b74e5d","cmd-6b905c787df94301","cmd-9cda3aaf6d6a4ed1","cmd-56901a32286a423c","cmd-455dafa59f914769","cmd-51c398282bbc4d19","cmd-f5a85b8ff1f94666","cmd-9744cfc605294a16"],"summary":"Confirmed NIC topology and paired transit/private networks via direct address ping tests before assigning final config"},{"requirement":"Bidirectional conn